1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,835
The sequence of tenses.

2
00:00:01,835 --> 00:00:07,578
When the main verb is in the past, the verb in the subordinate clause is normally past too.

3
00:00:07,578 --> 00:00:09,440
He said that he was unwell.

4
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:10,781
She asked what I wanted.

5
00:00:10,781 --> 00:00:12,786
They left before the guests arrived.

6
00:00:12,786 --> 00:00:29,166
Three exceptions: a universal truth stays present, he said that honesty is the best policy; a comparison after than may keep its own tense; and a present habit may be kept: she told me that she goes to the gym every morning.

